WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.652
In under two minutes, you will put your own lights on the map.

00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:04.684
We start on the map.

00:00:05.586 --> 00:00:08.918
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:10.932 --> 00:00:13.354
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.354 --> 00:00:15.844
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:17.190
Tap Use my location.

00:00:18.931 --> 00:00:21.147
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.147 --> 00:00:21.799
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.311 --> 00:00:27.807
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:27.807 --> 00:00:29.024
See the three dots?

00:00:29.024 --> 00:00:29.572
Tap them.

00:00:31.177 --> 00:00:32.756
In the menu, tap Add.

00:00:34.523 --> 00:00:35.940
Tap A lighting display.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.122
Who is posting?

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:40.415
Tap A homeowner.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:41.480
Then tap Next.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.612
Type the name to show.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:46.587
Then tap Next.

00:00:49.274 --> 00:00:51.509
Did a company install your lights?

00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:52.850
We did it ourselves.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.000
Tap No, then Next.

00:00:56.514 --> 00:00:57.481
Which season?

00:00:57.481 --> 00:00:59.207
Tap Christmas, then Next.

00:01:01.741 --> 00:01:05.103
Name the display, and tell us what makes it special.

00:01:05.103 --> 00:01:05.991
Then tap Next.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.467
Add the address.

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:13.971
The pin goes here.

00:01:13.971 --> 00:01:15.080
Then tap Next.

00:01:18.882 --> 00:01:22.410
Tell families when the lights are on, and how to see them.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.248
Then tap Next.

00:01:26.331 --> 00:01:27.493
Add photos.

00:01:27.493 --> 00:01:28.850
Then tap Next.

00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:34.167
Check everything, and tap Put it on the map.

00:01:36.199 --> 00:01:38.393
Next up: Find lights near you.
